On top of Peano, we have created multiple extensions which use this meshing
infrastructure for particular application domains: hyperbolic PDE solvers
(@ref page_exahype2_home), multigrid solvers (@ref page_multigrid_home) and
SPH (@ref page_exaparty_home, formerly known as Swift 2).
The @ref page_architecture_home "architecture page" provides an overview
including some illustrations.
The extensions are tools that allow you to write simulations for your
particular domain.
They are typically not "ready to use" products, even though some of them can
almost be used as such.

On top of these extensions, we in return implement various applications.
@ref page_exagrype (numerical general relativity) and
@ref applications_exahype2_exaseis (seismology) are popular examples.
You find more applications in the respective subdirectories.


<br /><br />
<div style="background-color: #cfc ; padding: 10px; border: 1px solid green;">
Peano (with any extension) is <b>not</b> a code. It is a tool to build your code.
However, some of the applications built on top of Peano with all its toolboxes and extensions provide "ready to use" options.
All components are integrated into one repository, one code base, and documented on these pages.
</div>



# Getting Peano

Peano is hosted on the
<a href="https://github.com/tobiasweinzierl/peano">GitHub</a>.
We do not provide regular snapshots.
Instead, clone the repository and use the latest version of the default branch
<tt>p4</tt>:

~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
git clone -b p4 https://github.com/tobiasweinzierl/peano.git
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~

Tagged versions are listed under
<a href="https://github.com/tobiasweinzierl/peano/tags">Tags</a> and
<a href="https://github.com/tobiasweinzierl/peano/releases">Releases</a>.
After that, follow the @ref page_installation_home "installation guide".
For HPC systems and reproducible environments, we also maintain
@ref page_installation_with_spack "Spack packages",
@ref page_installation_with_docker "Dockerfiles" and
@ref page_installation_with_apptainer "Apptainer definition files".


