<hr>

This is the documentation of Peano, generated automatically through Doxygen.
The latest version is published at
<a href="https://peano-framework.github.io/peano/">peano-framework.github.io/peano</a>.
To build it locally, run

~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
doxygen documentation/Doxyfile
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~

from the repository root.
The output is written to <tt>doxygen-html/html</tt>.
Peano comprises the core Peano 4 modules, the Python API, and a set of Peano
extensions as well as benchmarks.
The most important extensions at the moment are ExaHyPE 2, MGHyPE (our
multigrid and PETSc toolkit) and ExaParty.


# Citing Peano

Most users work with Peano through one of its Python APIs.
These generate the glue code and a makefile, plus a Readme file which lists
the Peano components that your code uses and the papers to cite for each of
them.
Please consult this file when you publish results.

If you want to cite Peano in general, please use

~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
@article{Weinzierl:2019:Peano,
  author  = {Weinzierl, Tobias},
  title   = {The Peano Software---Parallel, Automaton-based, Dynamically Adaptive Grid Traversals},
  journal = {ACM Transactions on Mathematical Software},
  volume  = {45},
  number  = {2},
  articleno = {14},
  year    = {2019},
  doi     = {10.1145/3319797}
}
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~

The file <tt>CITATION.cff</tt> in the repository root holds the citation
metadata of the software itself, including the list of contributors.


# Contributing, code of conduct and licence

Contributions are <b>welcome and very much appreciated</b>.
If you want to merge your work into the main code base, contact us and we will
give you write access to the repository.
The contribution guide <tt>CONTRIBUTING.md</tt> in the repository root and the
@ref page_developer_guidelines_home "developer guidelines" provide more details.
We follow a code of conduct (<tt>CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md</tt>).
Please follow its rules when participating in our community.

Peano is released under a modified BSD licence.
The full terms are in the file <tt>LICENSE</tt> in the repository root.

Peano has been awarded the
<a href="https://api.eu.badgr.io/public/assertions/uhyUShBWT1Wfd0Vx3EoMrQ">SQAaaS silver badge for software</a>.


